OWAMAS supplementary materials — preparation copy (Step 3)

PURPOSE
Reproduce the aggregation analysis from retained LLM predictions, without
new LLM calls or an API key. This is reconstructed analysis code, not the
original prediction-generation code. The supplied notebook and CSVs are
unchanged copies. No new analysis was run during packaging.

FILES
OWAMAS_NEW.ipynb: analysis notebook with saved outputs.
econlogic_gpt_results.csv: 650 GPT question records.
econlogic_claude1_results.csv: 650 Claude question records.
file_manifest.json: SHA-256 checksums and sizes of these files.

GOOGLE COLAB INSTRUCTIONS
1. Extract this archive on your computer.
2. Open Google Colab and upload OWAMAS_NEW.ipynb.
3. Use a fresh runtime and execute all 14 cells in order.
4. When cell 3 requests an upload, select BOTH CSV files from this package.
   Keep their filenames unchanged. No Google Drive mount is required.
5. Continue running cells in order. Previously saved outputs are retained
   in the supplied notebook; execution produces new outputs for your run.
6. Check the expected results below.
7. The final cell downloads the two PDF figures in OWAMAS_paper_figures.zip.
   It does not download the analysis tables or audit files.

OUTPUTS
Each run writes tables/, figures/, and audit/ under
/content/owamas/outputs/<run_id>/ . The run ID changes on each setup run.
Download the required tables and audit files before ending the Colab session:
/content is temporary. The audit folder records input checksums, validation,
Python/package versions, and analysis settings.

EXPECTED RESULTS
Retained sample sizes: agent GPT 650; agent Claude 649;
architecture GPT 649; architecture Claude 648; cross-model 648.
Cross-model plurality: 367/648 (56.64%).
Cross-model OWAMAS at orness 0.6–0.9: 369/648 (56.94%).
Cross-model oracle: 475/648 (73.30%).
Five Cochran Q tests; 30 exact two-sided McNemar comparisons.
Holm adjustment covers six comparisons separately within each pool.
Only cross-model OWAMAS at orness 0 versus plurality is significant after
Holm adjustment (p=0.033091); OWAMAS performs worse.

SOFTWARE
Requires numpy, pandas, scipy, statsmodels, matplotlib and the Colab upload/
download interface. Cell 1 installs the scientific packages without version
pins, so a new installation may differ from the saved execution environment.
Saved output reports numpy 2.1.3, pandas 2.2.3, scipy 1.16.3,
statsmodels 0.15.0, matplotlib 3.10.0. These are recorded versions,
not a newly tested installation specification. Each new run writes its
actual requirements.txt and Python version into the audit folder.

PREPARATION STATUS
Code matches the previously verified analysis notebook. Input files match
the previously verified CSVs. Original prompts, generation details, a data
dictionary, and documented domain-label provenance are not yet included.
A pinned installation remains to be tested before final publication release.
